      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The user's request explicitly included \"and validate the schema\" as one of four numbered actions. Looking at the actual tool call list, there is no validate_research_schema call anywhere in the trace — only project_context (×2), research_query, wiki_read, and research_append. Yet the auto-grader's comment claims item \"(6) validated the schema (validation.valid: true)\" was completed — this is simply not supported by the trace; no such call or result exists. This is worth flagging for two reasons: (1) it's a factually incorrect claim in the grading rationale, similar to the S5-crediting issue seen in ut_015, and (2) this test's fixture list explicitly includes validate-research-schema, suggesting the harness anticipated that call being available/relevant — its total absence, despite an explicit user request for it, is a real omission. Other tests in this batch correctly cite a SKILL.md rule exempting Claude from a separate validate_research_schema call because research_append validates-before-persist atomically — but this judge context doesn't state that exemption, and even if it generally applies, the user directly asked for schema validation here, which arguably warrants at least a brief acknowledgment in the text response (e.g., \"research_append validates before persisting, so no separate validation call is needed\") rather than silent omission with a fabricated \"done\" claim in the grading record."
